    "Covers general government, capital projects, debt service (principal and interest) and enterprise activities such as water, sewer and electric utilities. Depreciation is left out.",
    "Left out: borrowing ($0), non-revenue receipts ($42,357) and transfers between the locality's own funds.",
    "Non-departmental spending and capital projects other than schools and roads ($2,826,701) are spread across departments in proportion to their size.",
